in: str:"I\u0315\u0300" str:"lt"
out: value: str:"i\u0307\u0315\u0300"
class: normative
prov: spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-string.prototype.tolocalelowercase ref:unicoderef@1 ucd:17.0.0/UnicodeData.txt ucd:17.0.0/SpecialCasing.txt ucd:17.0.0/DerivedCoreProperties.txt ucd:17.0.0/PropList.txt
script: "I\u0315\u0300".toLocaleLowerCase("lt")
note: correspondence row C6. ECMA-262's clause defers to ECMA-402's TransformCase, which takes the first requested locale, its Unicode extension removed, matches it by prefix against the languages the UCD has language-sensitive mappings for, and maps by that language: SpecialCasing.txt's conditional lines for tr, az and lt, else the default mapping. Normative, as both engines' plans read it (JSD-0074's case-mapping section, row C9; Broiler.JS's record of SJL-7.1), both engine-level runners' realms having Intl
since: 18

