id: unicode/casing-folding/0001
area: unicode
op: RegExp ignoreCase, simple case folding
in: int:65 str:"iu" int:65 int:97 int:98
out: value: str:"true,true,false"
class: normative
prov: spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-runtime-semantics-canonicalize-ch spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-runtime-semantics-charactersetmatcher-abstract-operation spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-regexp.prototype.test ref:unicoderef@1 ucd:17.0.0/CaseFolding.txt
script: var r = /^\u0041$/iu; [r.test("A"), r.test("a"), r.test("b")].join()
note: the orbit U+0041 U+0061 and U+0062: under u or v, Canonicalize is simple case folding, so a code point matches every member of its orbit and nothing else
since: 18

